#: ../../source/user-guide/sparse-attention/cacheblend.md:13
msgid "🌟 What is CacheBlend?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/sparse-attention/cacheblend.md:15
msgid ""
"**CacheBlend** is a cached fusion system that combines multiple pre-"
"computed KV caches, when their corresponding texts are concatenated in "
"the LLM input. By selectively recomputing the KV cache values of a small "
"fraction of tokens,  CacheBlend reduces TTFT by 2.2 ~ 3.3× and increases "
"throughput by 2.8 ~ 5× under negligible quality drop."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/sparse-attention/cacheblend.md:18
msgid "🎯 Key Component"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/sparse-attention/cacheblend.md:20
msgid ""
"**🔍 Loading Controller**: the Loading Controller orchestrates which KV "
"caches to load, where from, and how much recomputation is needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/sparse-attention/cacheblend.md:21
msgid ""
"**⚡ KV Cache Store**: the KV Cache Store manages persistent storage, "
"lookup, and eviction of precomputed KV caches keyed by text-chunk "
"identity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/sparse-attention/cacheblend.md:22
msgid ""
"**🎛️ Cache Fusor**: the Fusor merges multiple chunk-level caches into one"
" coherent, cross-attention–correct KV cache, using minimal recomputation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/sparse-attention/cacheblend.md:24
msgid "🔥 Key Results"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/sparse-attention/cacheblend.md:25
msgid ""
"**2.2 ~ 3.3× speedup** of TTFT and **2.8 ~ 5× increase** of throughput "
"for long sequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/sparse-attention/cacheblend.md:26
msgid ""
"**Preserve High quality** no more than (1% ~ 3%) quality drop compared to"
" full KV recompute"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/sparse-attention/cacheblend.md:28
msgid "🧠 Ucm Implementation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/sparse-attention/cacheblend.md:30
msgid "Native Block-Wise Chunk KV Cache Dump, Load, PostProcess and Recompute"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/sparse-attention/cacheblend.md:31
msgid ""
"**🔐 Chunk Hash Encoding**: Similar as prefix hash, blend connector encode"
" the blocks of each chunk from the same hash meta beginning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/sparse-attention/cacheblend.md:32
msgid ""
"**⚡ Combine Prefix Cache and Chunk Cache**: Since chunk cache and native "
"prefix cache share the same hash space, they can be stored and shared in "
"a single store.When look up chunk cache, Blend connector first performs "
"prefix cache lookup to the fully reused part and then conduct chunk cache"
" lookup to fetch the candidate cache for blending."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/sparse-attention/cacheblend.md:33
msgid ""
"**🎯 Delta-Rope PostProcess**: Rectify the loaded chunk cache according to"
" their position in the new request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/sparse-attention/cacheblend.md:34
msgid ""
"**🔍 Integrate Cache Blend and First Token Generation**: Construct compute"
" mask of the HKVD tokens, cache miss tokens and suffix tokens, then "
"modify attention metadata to support the combination of chunk cache "
"blending, missing cache recomputing and first token generation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/user-guide/sparse-attention/cacheblend.md:35
msgid ""
"**🚀 Comprehensive Hook for LLM Forward Pipeline**: Based on and extended "
"from ucm sparse, blend sparse module reduces the input tokens for all the"
" computation kernel, not just the attention kernel."
msgstr ""

